# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder). The launchers do it for you.
#
# You probably do not need to edit anything here. The default is FULLY OFFLINE
# (Ollama on this computer): no key, no account, no internet, and no question
# ever leaves the machine. Searching the archive is offline either way.
#
# Only fill something in if you deliberately want to send questions to a cloud
# provider instead -- the app's Settings panel writes this file for you.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Option 1 (DEFAULT): fully offline, no key, no internet ----------------
# Install Ollama from https://ollama.com/download and the app starts it for
# you. The macOS launcher offers to download the model on first run; to do it
# by hand:  ollama pull qwen2.5:3b-instruct
#
# These are the defaults already -- uncomment only to change them.
# ASSISTANT_MODEL_PROVIDER=ollama
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b-instruct
#
# 3b, not 7b: on the reference M1, 7b's prompt prefill alone was ~50s. Set
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b-instruct only on a machine with headroom.
# The first question after opening the app is slow (~70s measured) while the
# model loads into RAM; later questions land in ~13s.

# --- Option 2: Google Gemini ------------------------------------------------
# Questions are sent to Google. Free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# ASSISTANT_MODEL_PROVIDER=google_genai
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Option 3: Anthropic Claude ---------------------------------------------
# Questions are sent to Anthropic. Key from console.anthropic.com
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ASSISTANT_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# --- Option 4: OpenAI --------------------------------------------------------
# Questions are sent to OpenAI. Key from platform.openai.com
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ASSISTANT_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tuning (optional -- the defaults are measured values, not guesses.
# Read the comments in pakpatat/config.py before changing any of them.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The anti-guessing gate. If the best archive match scores below this, the
# assistant refuses to answer instead of improvising.
#   Raise  (e.g. 0.35) = stricter, says "not in the archive" more often
#   Lower  (e.g. 0.20) = more willing to attempt an answer
# ASSISTANT_MIN_SCORE=0.28

# How many archive passages to feed the model per question.
# ASSISTANT_TOP_K=8

# Context window for local models. Ollama's own default is 4096 and it
# truncates SILENTLY past it -- which on this corpus was already dropping
# source text on common questions. Do not lower this.
# ASSISTANT_NUM_CTX=8192
